{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.GSReductionOrder","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GSReductionOrder","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CrystalGraphRealization"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GSOrderMatch.canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GSOrderMatch.canonical","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GSReductionOrder.lean#L128-L161","doc":"**The trivial model — a `def`, not an `instance`, and not \"faithful\".**\n\nIts docstring said *\"Faithful instance. Carries the explicit research-grade\nconjecture as a sorry.\"* Neither half was true. There is no `sorry`: it sets\n`NormalForm := PUnit` and both `confinementLevel _ := 0` and\n`crystalDeg _ := 0`, so the order-match (★) is discharged by `rfl` on\n`0 = 0`. Two filtrations agree because both are identically zero on a\none-element set of normal forms, not because the GS reduction order tracks\nthe KLR grading. A `sorry` would at least be visible to `#print axioms`;\nthis was not.\n\nThe class docstring calls `order_match` \"the `sorry`-equivalent the whole\n`crystal-graph-realization` chain reduces to\". That is the right reading of\nthe *class*; this model was what stopped it from being true of the corpus,\nbecause as an unconditional `instance` it discharged that field for every\n`R` and `q` and made `confinement_eq_crystalDeg` an unconditional theorem\nabout the zero filtration.\n\nSame shape as `ConfinementGradingCorrespondence.canonical`, which states\nthe same correspondence over `[CrystalGraphRealization R q]`, and demoted\nthe same way (bean `qou-fngs`). Nothing consumed it: the class has no users\noutside this file.\n\n**Still open:** (★) itself — that `crystalDeg T = confinementLevel T` on the\n`n!` genuine GS normal forms, on the nose rather than up to a re-indexing of\nstrata. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GSOrderMatch.confinement_eq_crystalDeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GSOrderMatch.confinement_eq_crystalDeg","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GSReductionOrder.lean#L118-L126","doc":"Unconditional downstream restatement: under the order-match, the\nconfinement filtration is exactly the KLR `ℤ`-grading filtration —\nthe content `conj:confinement-grading-correspondence` needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GSOrderMatch.order_match","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GSOrderMatch.order_match","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GSReductionOrder.lean#L114-L114","doc":"**The conjecture (★)**: the GS reduction order matches the KLR\ngrading filtration on the nose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GSOrderMatch.crystalDeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GSOrderMatch.crystalDeg","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GSReductionOrder.lean#L111-L111","doc":"Brundan–Kleshchev KLR ℤ-grading degree of a normal form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GSOrderMatch.confinementLevel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GSOrderMatch.confinementLevel","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GSReductionOrder.lean#L109-L109","doc":"LP shadow-price confinement level of a normal form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GSOrderMatch.NormalForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GSOrderMatch.NormalForm","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GSReductionOrder.lean#L107-L107","doc":"Abstract type of GS normal forms `T_w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GSOrderMatch.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GSOrderMatch.mk","kind":"ctor","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GSReductionOrder.lean#L105-L105","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GSOrderMatch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GSOrderMatch","kind":"class","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GSReductionOrder.lean#L91-L114","doc":"**GS ↔ KLR order-match (conjecture, axiomatised).**\n\nPairs the GS reduction order with the KLR `ℤ`-grading. The fields:\n- `NormalForm` — the GS normal forms (abstractly, the `n!` reduced\n  words `T_w`);\n- `confinementLevel` — the LP shadow-price confinement level\n  (`def:confinement-level`);\n- `crystalDeg` — the Brundan–Kleshchev KLR `ℤ`-grading degree;\n- `order_match` — **the conjecture (★)**: on every GS normal form the\n  two filtrations agree *on the nose*, `crystalDeg = confinementLevel`,\n  rather than only up to a re-indexing of strata. This single field is\n  the `sorry`-equivalent the whole `crystal-graph-realization` chain\n  reduces to. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.h3_nf_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.h3_nf_card","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GSReductionOrder.lean#L83-L87","doc":"The `Hₙ(q)` GS normal-form basis has `n!` elements (Diamond-Lemma\ncount). Recorded here at `n = 3` as a machine-checked sanity anchor,\nmatching `nf_basis3_card` in the `hecke-normal-form` sibling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Reduced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Reduced","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GSReductionOrder.lean#L79-L81","doc":"A word is **GS-reduced** when no rewrite step applies — these are the\nGröbner–Shirshov irreducible normal forms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Step.yangBaxter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Step.yangBaxter","kind":"ctor","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GSReductionOrder.lean#L75-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Step.farComm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Step.farComm","kind":"ctor","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GSReductionOrder.lean#L73-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Step.hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Step.hecke","kind":"ctor","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GSReductionOrder.lean#L71-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Step","kind":"inductive","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GSReductionOrder.lean#L52-L77","doc":"The Gröbner–Shirshov single-step rewrite relation of\n`def:hecke-normal-form`, on the reduced-word combinatorics:\n\n* `hecke`     — the quadratic collision `σ_i σ_i`; the Hecke relation\n                `σ_i² = (q−q⁻¹)σ_i + 1` removes the `σ_i σ_i` factor\n                from any *reduced* word (its linear tail is tracked\n                separately in `hecke-normal-form.lean`);\n* `farComm`   — far-commutativity oriented to move the smaller index\n                left, `σ_i σ_j → σ_j σ_i` when `j + 2 ≤ i`; the single\n                orientation (not the symmetric `|i−j| ≥ 2`) keeps the\n                step strictly shortlex-decreasing, so the relation\n                terminates instead of looping `i::j ↔ j::i`;\n* `yangBaxter`— the braid move oriented shortlex-decreasing,\n                `σ_{i+1} σ_i σ_{i+1} → σ_i σ_{i+1} σ_i` (the rewrite\n                lowers the leading generator index from `i+1` to `i`).\n\nConfluence is the Diamond Lemma (Bergman 1978); the normal forms\nbiject with `Sₙ` (`n!` of them). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GSWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GSWord","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GSReductionOrder.lean#L48-L50","doc":"A GS word over the braid generators: `σ_i` is encoded by its index\n`i : ℕ`, and a word is the list of generator indices. ","signatureChunk":0}]}